ing was generally well organized, turnout was high, and Erdoğan required a runoff."]},{"evidence_id":"E076","claim":"The European Commission found continued backsliding in expression, assembly, association, judicial independence, and treatment of critical voices, including during the 2023 election campaign.","publisher":"ab.gov.tr","publication_date":"unknown_not_exposed_by_source","source_confidence":"unknown_not_recorded","period_fit":"unknown_not_recorded","ruler_attribution":"unknown_not_recorded","contrary_evidence":[]},{"evidence_id":"E079","claim":"The presidential constitutional system centralized policymaking and regulatory authority, weakened separation of powers, and left executive accountability operating mainly through elections.","publisher":"ab.gov.tr","publication_date":"unknown_not_exposed_by_source","source_confidence":"unknown_not_recorded","period_fit":"unknown_not_recorded","ruler_attribution":"unknown_not_recorded","contrary_evidence":[]},{"evidence_id":"E080","claim":"Erdoğan was re-elected in the May 2023 presidential election, the ruling coalition retained a parliamentary majority, and the European Commission found genuine alternatives and high participation but biased media coverage and an uneven field favoring the incumbent.","publisher":"ab.gov.tr","publication_date":"unknown_not_exposed_by_source","source_confidence":"unknown_not_recorded","period_fit":"unknown_not_recorded","ruler_attribution":"unknown_not_recorded","contrary_evidence":[]}]}
